  "releaseNotes": "- Discovers nested Skill entries and imports multi-Skill archives without\n  restructuring packages, preserving relative references, scripts and assets\n- Tracks physical package ownership separately from Skill names, with\n  independent entry activation and complete-package replacement and export\n- Keeps package deletion atomic and rejects partial nested-entry deletion that\n  could break shared resources; archive safety checks and rollback remain\n- Gives Codex and OpenCode the same resolved native catalog while staging\n  complete source packages outside native discovery, avoiding duplicate entries\n- Preserves shared and private workspace checkpointing, binary resources and\n  executable scripts, without modifying global originals\n- Displays package-relative entry paths in the existing Skills settings rows\n  without adding import or delete controls to the management page\n- Reuses Runtime `1.0.0-beta.28`; no template rebuild is required, and existing\n  configuration, conversations, attachments and durable workspace data remain",
